  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 110 PM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nThe front will either be entirely through or through the vast \nmajority of South Central Texas by sunrise Friday morning as it \ntracks south across the state. Northerly wind quickly increases \nbehind this feature while temperatures rapidly cool. \n\nThere remains some variance in models on exactly how cool air behind \nthe front is but hi-res guidance seems to favor a cooler solution \nthan the global ensembles; therefore, have trended slightly cooler \nthan the NBM with this update. Highs somewhere in the 60s north to \npossibly low 80s south are forecast Friday with windy conditions \nthrough the day. Gusty wind will gusts as high as 40 mph are \nexpected Friday into Saturday morning, with a gradual weakening of \nwinds Saturday into Sunday. A Wind Advisory during this time may be \nissued. Cooler and more Fall-like weather stick around through \nMonday morning with highs in the 60s or 70s and lows in the 40s or \n50s. \n\nEnsemble guidance brings back warmer highs and lows for the start of \nthe week into the mid-week period with some low PoPs over the area. \nRidging is favored to build over the area during this time ahead of \nanother trough in the west.",
